{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/862232-which-colors-of-magic-the-gathering-represent-each-splat","id":862232,"title":"Which Colors Of Magic: The Gathering Represent Each Splat?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-08T15:49:12-07:00","id":862232,"title":"Which Colors Of Magic: The Gathering Represent Each Splat?","content":"I'm gonna play it by ear, so don't take this first shot at it too seriously.<br /> <br /> Vampire: Red/Black<br /> Werewolf: Red/Green<br /> Mage: Blue/White<br /> Promethean: Red/Black<br /> Changeling: Green/Blue<br /> Hunter: White/Red<br /> Geist: Green/Black<br /> Mummy: White/Black<br /> Demon: Blue/Black<br /> Beast: Red/Green<br /> <br /> As for the fan splats, I'd say Genius is Blue/White. Leviathan is Black/Blue and Princess is White/Green.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T15:53:50-07:00","id":862235,"title":"","content":"I'd argue that Mummies are some combination of Green, Black, and White. Green is honestly their primary color; it governs life magic (remember that the Arisen are Deathless immortals, not Lifeless horrors) and the power of tradition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T15:56:56-07:00","id":862237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/862232-which-colors-of-magic-the-gathering-represent-each-splat#post862232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf: Red/Green</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting you say this because just recently we got a Werewolf Planeswalker with the same colors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=410007\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://gatherer-static.wizards.com/Cards/medium/35D779A6BFF3C645393C0B9B2E5B1509AA21B37CFA9096DA41C9315382E996DA.webp\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=410007\" target=\"_blank\"> Arlinn Kord MTG - Shadows over Innistrad #243 (English) | Magic: The Gathering </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=410007\" target=\"_blank\"> http://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=410007 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Official MTG details and rulings for Arlinn Kord, Legendary Planeswalker &ndash; Arlinn from SOI (243) (English). Read official rules and rulings directly from Magic: The Gathering. </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T16:08:48-07:00","id":862247,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/862232-which-colors-of-magic-the-gathering-represent-each-splat?p=862235#post862235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue that Mummies are some combination of Green, Black, and White. Green is honestly their primary color; it governs life magic (remember that the Arisen are Deathless immortals, not Lifeless horrors) and the power of tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's a good point. I said White because it's all about law and righteousness, which resonates with the Arisen and the Obrimos. I mention that Path because one of their Ruling Arcana, Prime, can also affect symbolic laws, and is hypothesized by some to be connected with Sekhem. So Mummies might be a White/Green with a strong bent toward Lawful Evil.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/862232-which-colors-of-magic-the-gathering-represent-each-splat?p=862237#post862237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting you say this because just recently we got a Werewolf Planeswalker with the same colors.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=410007\" target=\"_blank\">http://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Ca...verseid=410007</a></div> </div> </div> </div> Interesting. Does he have two powers instead of three because he's dichromatic? The Planeswalkers I'm familiar with were all monochromatic with three powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T16:13:40-07:00","id":862251,"title":"","content":"I'd argue Prometheans are White/Red and Hunters are White/Black. The Promethean condition itself is very much trying to understand Red and White concepts while embodying their negative aspects (and trying to reach a harmonious whole), while Hunter is all about using whatever means they have at their disposal to strike back against their foes, using self-determination (Black) to protect the community (White).<br /> <br /> I'd say Mummies are Green/Black (focus on the cycle of life and death and its exceptions, balancing predetermination with self-determination), while Geists are White/Black, but from a completely different perspective from Hunters. In this case, White/Black as spirituality, taking both the religious side of White with Black's take on death and the dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T16:18:39-07:00","id":862255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/862232-which-colors-of-magic-the-gathering-represent-each-splat?p=862247#post862247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[<br /> Interesting. Does he have two powers instead of three because he's dichromatic? The Planeswalkers I'm familiar with were all monochromatic with three powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>She has five powers. the card is double-faced. She's also red/green because those are the werewolf colours in Magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T16:29:52-07:00","id":862260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/862232-which-colors-of-magic-the-gathering-represent-each-splat?p=862255#post862255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She has five powers. the card is double-faced. She's also red/green because those are the werewolf colours in Magic.</div> </div> </div> </div> Weird. The page on my computer only loaded the front of her card. I hit F5 and her werewolf form showed up. Connection problems, I guess.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T16:31:07-07:00","id":862262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/862232-which-colors-of-magic-the-gathering-represent-each-splat?p=862251#post862251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue Prometheans are White/Red and Hunters are White/Black. The Promethean condition itself is very much trying to understand Red and White concepts while embodying their negative aspects (and trying to reach a harmonious whole), while Hunter is all about using whatever means they have at their disposal to strike back against their foes, using self-determination (Black) to protect the community (White).<br /> <br /> I'd say Mummies are Green/Black (focus on the cycle of life and death and its exceptions, balancing predetermination with self-determination), while Geists are White/Black, but from a completely different perspective from Hunters. In this case, White/Black as spirituality, taking both the religious side of White with Black's take on death and the dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummies need some White in their color identity because their lives revolve around enforcing divine laws. Like I said, the most accurate portrait of Mummies would be Abzan colors (W/B/G), but if they have to stay two-color than they're definitely W/G.<br /> <br /> Bonus points for that being the color combo used for weenie token decks, so as to best represent their Cults!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T16:34:05-07:00","id":862263,"title":"","content":"Fair enough! I'm not well-versed in Mummy, so I concede to the superior expertise.<br /> <br /> I am pleased beyond thought that my favourite colour combination (Blue/Green) is also the best match for my favourite gameline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T16:34:32-07:00","id":862265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/862232-which-colors-of-magic-the-gathering-represent-each-splat?p=862251#post862251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue Prometheans are White/Red and Hunters are White/Black. The Promethean condition itself is very much trying to understand Red and White concepts while embodying their negative aspects (and trying to reach a harmonious whole), while Hunter is all about using whatever means they have at their disposal to strike back against their foes, using self-determination (Black) to protect the community (White).<br /> <br /> I'd say Mummies are Green/Black (focus on the cycle of life and death and its exceptions, balancing predetermination with self-determination), while Geists are White/Black, but from a completely different perspective from Hunters. In this case, White/Black as spirituality, taking both the religious side of White with Black's take on death and the dead.</div> </div> </div> </div> These are all very accurate summations. Have a Like. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T16:37:56-07:00","id":862266,"title":"","content":"You could make an argument for beasts being Blue because Blue is the mind magic colour and beasts are astral-based. It's also the giant sea monster colour, so Makara are going to want some at least.<br /> <br /> Promethan may also want some Blue, because that's the allotted &quot;Frankenstein's monster&quot; colour, at least on Innistrad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T16:47:38-07:00","id":862272,"title":"","content":"Blue also fits Promethean because it's the colour of learning and progress. If we're going three-colours, I'd say:<br /> <br /> Vampire: Red/Black/Blue.<br /> Werewolf: Red/Green/White.<br /> Mage: Blue/White/Black.<br /> Promethean: Red/White/Blue.<br /> Changeling: Green/Blue/Red.<br /> Hunter: White/Black/Red.<br /> Geist: White/Black/Blue.<br /> Mummy: Green/White/Black.<br /> Demon: Blue/Black/White.<br /> Beast: Black/Red/Blue.<br /> Deviant: Blue/Green/Black.<br /> <br /> Fansplats:<br /> <br /> Genius: Blue/Red/White.<br /> Leviathan: Black/Blue/Green.<br /> Princess: White/Green/Red.<br /> <br /> Coincidences:<br /> <br /> Beast and Vampire, Mage and Geist and Demon, Werewolf and Princess (!), Deviant and Leviathan, Genius and Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":10056,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","user":"ShadowKnight1224","date":". 04-08-2016, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T16:56:59-07:00","id":862277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/862232-which-colors-of-magic-the-gathering-represent-each-splat?p=862266#post862266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could make an argument for beasts being Blue because Blue is the mind magic colour and beasts are astral-based. It's also the giant sea monster colour, so Makara are going to want some at least.<br /> <br /> Promethan may also want some Blue, because that's the allotted &quot;Frankenstein's monster&quot; colour, at least on Innistrad.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't know, Atavisms and Nightmares scream Black to me. I just didn't feel like saying Red/Black a third time, so I picked Green to represent the focus on Kinship.<br /> <br /> And I'd say Blue is closer to the mindset of the people that start Lineages. &quot;<b><i>IT'S ALIIIIIIIIIIIIIVE!!!!</i></b>&quot; and all that jazz. But Shadowknight1224 has a point about Blue representing learning and progress. So Prometheans might be Red/Blue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-08-2016, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T17:17:36-07:00","id":862287,"title":"","content":"Oh, nightmares are certainly Black, but they're also a bit Blue. They sort of sit right where the two colours collide. Regardless, I meant Beasts are blue for the same reasons Nicol Bolas is Red. It's not really to do with their MO, it's just a function of what they are. Bolas is a dragon, so he's Red. Beasts are astral monsters, so they'll be Blue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T10:49:55-07:00","id":862656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/862232-which-colors-of-magic-the-gathering-represent-each-splat?p=862287#post862287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, nightmares are certainly Black, but they're also a bit Blue. They sort of sit right where the two colours collide. Regardless, I meant Beasts are blue for the same reasons Nicol Bolas is Red. It's not really to do with their MO, it's just a function of what they are. Bolas is a dragon, so he's Red. Beasts are astral monsters, so they'll be Blue.</div> </div> </div> </div> Alright, that makes sense. So, if I chose two colors for Beasts following function instead of modus operandi, they would be Blue/Black, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T11:15:36-07:00","id":862665,"title":"","content":"The thing about Magic's color pie is that it's so archetypal that any sufficiently complex character will have aspects of all five colors. For example, look at vampire. The overall concept is based in black, with maybe some red in the form of Frenzy, but each Clan is a color. Daeva are passionate and physical, as red as they come. Gangrel are driven by instinct and connected with their animal natures, which is very much green. Mekhet are all about knowledge and secrets, they're definitely blue. Nosferatu are all about fear which is a big theme in black. And Ventrue are a perfect example of the negative side of white.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T12:29:17-07:00","id":862697,"title":"","content":"I love idea of Black White Ventrue. I remember that BW had some nice OBEY board domination feel to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T13:01:43-07:00","id":862714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/862232-which-colors-of-magic-the-gathering-represent-each-splat?p=862665#post862665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about Magic's color pie is that it's so archetypal that any sufficiently complex character will have aspects of all five colors. For example, look at vampire. The overall concept is based in black, with maybe some red in the form of Frenzy, but each Clan is a color. Daeva are passionate and physical, as red as they come. Gangrel are driven by instinct and connected with their animal natures, which is very much green. Mekhet are all about knowledge and secrets, they're definitely blue. Nosferatu are all about fear which is a big theme in black. And Ventrue are a perfect example of the negative side of white.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well said. You could make a similar case for Mage as a whole being primarily Blue. However, since each Path has two Ruling Arcana that are intimately connected, you'll leave out important aspects if you choose only one color. So here goes:<br /> <br /> Acanthus = Blue/Green<br /> Mastigos = Black/Blue<br /> Moros = Blue/Black<br /> Obrimos = White/Red<br /> Thyrsus = Green/Red","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T13:06:40-07:00","id":862716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/862232-which-colors-of-magic-the-gathering-represent-each-splat?p=862714#post862714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well said. You could make a similar case for Mage as a whole being primarily Blue. However, since each Path has two Ruling Arcana that are intimately connected, you'll leave out important aspects if you choose only one color. So here goes:<br /> <br /> Acanthus = Blue/Green<br /> Mastigos = Red/Black<br /> Moros = Black/Blue<br /> Obrimos = White/Red<br /> Thyrsus = Green/Red</div> </div> </div> </div>I have long wanted to create a Magic the Gathering themed setting hack for Awakening where the colors are paths, but so much of Mage is just so blue it's like I'm listening to Eifel65.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T13:25:06-07:00","id":862730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/862232-which-colors-of-magic-the-gathering-represent-each-splat?p=862716#post862716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have long wanted to create a Magic the Gathering themed setting hack for Awakening where the colors are paths, but so much of Mage is just so blue it's like I'm listening to Eifel65.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;I have a blue Ward on my blue Cabal.<br /> Blue is the colour of all that I cast.<br /> Blue are the Realms and all the Paths are too.<br /> I have a student, and she is so blue.<br /> Blue are the Sleepers here that walk around,<br /> Blue like my Nimbus, it's in and outside.<br /> Blue are the words I say and what I think.<br /> Blue are the Symbols that live inside me.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T14:47:27-07:00","id":862772,"title":"","content":"Awakening U<br /> Enchantment - Aura<br /> Enchant Creature<br /> Enchanted creature is a Wizard in addition to it's other types.<br /> Enchanted Creature has prowess.<br /> When enchanted creature deals combat damage to a player, investigate.<br /> <br /> Lorehouse 2<br /> Artifact<br /> At the beginning of each player's upkeep, that player investigates.<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"color:#444444\">(Put a colorless Clue artifact token onto the battlefield with&quot;{2}, sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.&quot;)<br /> <br /> Athaneum Curator 2U{W/B}<br /> Creature - Human Wizard<br /> Prowess<br /> When Athaenum Curator enters the battlefield, each activated ability of Clues you control costs {2} less to activate until end of turn.<br /> 2/3<br /> <br /> None of these are particularly inspired, I'm out of practice.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:04:49-07:00","id":862786,"title":"","content":"I would say Awakening should give the creature T: Investigate instead of triggering it off combat damage, but that would be pretty anti-synergistic with Prowess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T22:20:41-07:00","id":863023,"title":"","content":"For me, Unchained are pretty clearly Red/Blue as a species. They want the ability to <i>choose </i>above all else (even Integrators, who want a better way of serving God than what they were given), and to act according to their hearts. They do so via subterfuge, planning, and the acquisition of knowledge. Inquisitors are heavy on the Blue, Saboteurs on the Red, Integrators have a tinge of White in their beliefs, and how much White and Black a Tempter has varies from Builder to Builder. Not one of them has a single leaf of Green, though-natural instinct, simply accepting the nature of things, and naivety is something an Unchained who survives finds utterly inexplicable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T22:27:19-07:00","id":863025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/862232-which-colors-of-magic-the-gathering-represent-each-splat?p=863023#post863023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, Unchained are pretty clearly Red/Blue as a species. They want the ability to <i>choose </i>above all else (even Integrators, who want a better way of serving God than what they were given), and to act according to their hearts. They do so via subterfuge, planning, and the acquisition of knowledge. Inquisitors are heavy on the Blue, Saboteurs on the Red, Integrators have a tinge of White in their beliefs, and how much White and Black a Tempter has varies from Builder to Builder. Not one of them has a single leaf of Green, though-natural instinct, simply accepting the nature of things, and naivety is something an Unchained who survives finds utterly inexplicable.</div> </div> </div> </div> You could have a few environmentally conscious Tempters, geo-politician and sociologist Inquisitors and eco-terrorist Saboteurs. They might say something like &quot;what's the use of freeing the world from the God-Machine if we'll just ruin it ourselves in a few generations?&quot;<br /> <br /> Everything else you said is very accurate, though. Have a Like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T22:51:00-07:00","id":863033,"title":"","content":"I would argue that the Unchained's drive for autonomy is ultimately more black than red. Personal freedom is important to red, but ultimately red is defined by emotion. Conversely, amorality may be the first thing that comes to mind in association with black, but if Mark Rosewater's articles on color philosophy are any indication, black's single most fundamental value is individualism (though white might call it selfishness).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T00:38:19-07:00","id":863063,"title":"","content":"Genius: I'd say Blue/Red with Blue being Obligation and Red being madness.<br /> <br /> Princess I'd say is White/Red; balancing out White's focus on community and law with Red's focus on freedom and emotions to bring out the best of both colours.<br /> <br /> Leviathan is Green with an focus on the status quo, instinct and their own small social group; not that Leviathans like the status quo. It has shades of Black from the Divine Nature's amoral selfishness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T07:48:35-07:00","id":863150,"title":"","content":"I'd say Beast is Green because the horror is instinctual and savage; Blue, for their mind powers; Black, for their manipulation of fear and selfish attitudes. So, Sultai, which really fits the Beast themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T09:30:45-07:00","id":863190,"title":"","content":"I guess if we're including Fansplats, well I can shamelessly self advertise (mostly a joke) , Monarch would be Green/White with some Blue leanings.<br /> <br /> We are talking about alien-terran-hybrids that lord over thousands of lesser nonsentinent creatures, held in check by rigid fuedal society and rules but capable of some abilities normally reserved for blue. There's an emphasis on numbers mattering, as well as maintaining logistics between your realm... so that when your betters come knocking you can pay them off.<br /> <br /> <br /> Inheritance Dragons are Red. No doubt about it. I just don't know what the other colors are. Green maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T10:17:54-07:00","id":863210,"title":"","content":"If it's fine that I do a tiny bit of self-advertizing as well, I think that Siren would be Green/White with a touch of Red. They're focused on stopping the Deluge from coming, healing the troubles inflicted that could result in it coming and trying to guide people down a better path. The touch of Red is from their relationship to humanity, like Ariel loving the Prince from afar and throwing consequences to the wind, only to suffer when he loves another and dies in the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T20:11:47-07:00","id":863452,"title":"","content":"I haven't played Magic in a long time, and now I hear of both this topic and a werewolf planeswalker? This must be one of the better weekends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T20:47:45-07:00","id":863465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryphon's Feather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/862232-w